# Delivery Gate: configuration reference. Copy to .env and fill in ONLY if you want live extraction.
#
# The application reads the PROCESS ENVIRONMENT. It does not load .env files by itself.
# To use a .env file in a POSIX shell:   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# Nothing here is required. With neither variable set, the app runs entirely offline on fixtures,
# and the 15 built-in sample documents are read from recorded extraction outputs.

# --- Optional: live evidence extraction (a provider key AND a model are both required) ----------------------------
# Recommended provider: Groq (see docs/GROQ.md). Get a key at https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key-here
# The model identifier. NO default is built in, because Groq retires models every few months. As of Nov 12, 2026 the recommended
# Production models are openai/gpt-oss-120b and openai/gpt-oss-20b. Run `python3 -m delivery_extraction.groq_check` to confirm
# your choice is available to your account before a demo. Retired examples to avoid: llama-3.3-70b-versatile, llama-3.1-8b-instant.
EXTRACTION_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# Optional: low (default), medium or high. Only sent to the two gpt-oss models.
# EXTRACTION_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# Optional: force a provider (groq or anthropic). If unset: Groq when GROQ_API_KEY is set, otherwise Anthropic when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set.
# EXTRACTION_PROVIDER=groq
# Alternative provider (still supported): an Anthropic key instead of a Groq key, with an Anthropic model name in EXTRACTION_MODEL.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key-here
# The keys are read server-side only and are never sent to the browser (tests check this).

# --- Server address (command-line flags, not environment variables) ---------------------------------
#   python3 -m delivery_ui --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
# Defaults: host 127.0.0.1, port 8080. The demo is not hardened for exposure beyond localhost.

# --- Optional: read-only PayPal SANDBOX check (separate command-line tool; see docs/PAYPAL_SANDBOX.md) --------
# Sandbox REST app credentials from https://developer.paypal.com (Apps & Credentials, Sandbox tab).
# These are SANDBOX credentials only. The client can only contact api-m.sandbox.paypal.com and cannot move money.
PAYPAL_SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID=your-sandbox-client-id-here
PAYPAL_SANDBOX_CLIENT_SECRET=your-sandbox-client-secret-here
